  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Replacing Si or Mn with Al in CrFeCoNiX alloys promotes formation of a stable, coherent Al2O3 surface layer above 900 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al oxidizes preferentially in these alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3 formed is tightly adherent and has low diffusivity.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using Si or Mn as X produces less protective, more defect-prone oxides than using Al.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxide scales formed on the Si- or Mn-containing alloys tend to crack or spall.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Favorable oxidation thermodynamics cause Al to form a continuous Al2O3 layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Low oxygen diffusivity through Al2O3 contributes to its protective behavior.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3 layer minimizes internal stresses in the oxide scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Minimizing internal stresses prevents crack propagation and spallation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si- or Mn-derived oxides have higher defect densities and faster diffusion than the Al-derived oxide.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher defect densities and faster diffusion make the Si- or Mn-derived oxide layers unstable.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al-containing alloys will exhibit a more stable and continuous protective oxide scale than otherwise comparable Si- or Mn-containing alloys.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective scale on the Al-containing alloy will resist cracking and spallation better than scales on the Si- or Mn-containing controls.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed behavior applies above 900 °C in oxidative or corrosive atmospheres while the materials maintain a metallic solid-solution state.",
